WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.070
Please put my Macbeth to an end.

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.150
That's impossible.

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:08.990
Macbeth has been incorporated into tonight's play.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:11.530
Are you sure you want me to be the star?

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.330
You're trying to annoy me, aren't you?

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:14.910
Which are you?

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.330
What do you mean?

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:22.170
From the orphanage ten years ago.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:23.920
Which one of the girls are you?

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.010
You can't tell?

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:28.260
Judge. I cannot.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:31.140
Because you were the only one there,

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.640
Thomas No.14 Shakespeare.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:39.020
It was just me?

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:39.940
Right.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:44.150
But I will fulfill the promise I made to both versions of you.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:45.730
I am going to write again.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:48.950
I will write about the world's boundaries.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:50.450
That is pointless.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.370
It's fine as long as I'm having fun.

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:57.040
It'd be even better if readers who love books picked it up and enjoyed it.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:03.670
And I'll go to where you are, where you get showered in critiques and discussed at length.

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:10.220
In that case, if I should win, stay in England and figure out which one is me.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:19.560
Go, army of Birnam!

00:02:58.990 --> 00:02:59.910
Tenzo!

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.870
C-Cecil, crush them!

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:06.120
May God be with you!

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.930
Tenzo, I'll let you owe me one!

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.800
H-How foolhardy!

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:19.930
I'm well aware!

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:22.680
Back in elementary school when you said

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.390
"You kind of smell like a dog,"

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:28.270
I thought that you would
be my life-long enemy.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:29.690
I don't remember that!

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:30.980
You truly are the worst!

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:35.450
<i>But there is something I remember as well, Tenzo.</i>

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:38.110
<i>You were wary of me, weren't you?</i>

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.580
<i>When everyone would get together,</i>

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:43.120
<i>you never left me out of the fun.</i>

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:45.200
<i>I'm not the type to forget that.</i>

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.710
<i>So as an adult capable of bearing weight,</i>

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:50.420
<i>I'll bear yours since you're a novice at it!</i>

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.800
Tenzo, you have three minutes to get your girl!

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:53.380
Judge!

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:56.260
F-Fire!

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:06.730
We've won this time... because that moron is a ninja!

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:11.980
C-Cecil, we should finish off the enemy that's still here!

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:12.650
Tes!

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:15.990
Squash!

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.540
Kimi! Why are you here?!

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.330
To enjoy the night.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:35.760
Miss Iron Balls and Miss Balloon,

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.800
you look as if you have a question.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:39.340
I'm willing to answer it!

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:42.180
You have one second! One! Okay, time's up!

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:43.430
Now I won't answer your questions.

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:45.470
G-Give us more time!

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:49.390
The sun is setting, even though the night has already fallen.

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:53.110
H-How are you able to ignore Cecil's weight?

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:54.230
Idiot!

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:57.030
There's no way I would explain that to my enemies.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.150
How?

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.160
Even you don't get why?

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:04.030
Fine, I'll tell you!

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:08.500
My God accepts makeup and fashion as ritual offerings.

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:12.960
In other words, I'm impervious to almost any spell simply by being me!

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:14.880
It's a trade secret!

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:16.300
<i>Sh-She just readily told us!</i>

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:21.880
Now then, we'll deal with you two quickly.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:24.470
H-How dare you say that?!

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.060
Don't get any funny ideas.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:29.930
Despite how it may seem, I'm in a pretty good mood.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:36.650
After all, my Foolish Brother and his future wife have decided their futures, even if they're awkward about it.

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:38.650
London is a nice city, isn't it?

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:41.400
So I'll let you off with merely beating you to a pulp.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:43.780
Wha—

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:46.330
Move forward, Malga Naruze.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:47.330
What?

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:51.120
This ought to help you release some of your stress.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:09.100
I now declare the second battle against the Spanish Armada over.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:13.900
We will take time to fuel before commencing the third skirmish, the Battle of Calais.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:19.030
Th-Third battle? Fueling time?

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:24.320
We determine the Battle of Portland was cleared the moment we bombarded them.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:28.450
Next, Tres España should begin fueling their ships. Over.

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:33.540
During the upcoming Battle of Calais,

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:38.790
eight of England's fire ships will charge into
Tres España's armada and send them into turmoil.

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:43.260
In all reality, the flow of the battle against the Spanish Armada has been predetermined.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:47.470
But weren't you supposed to carry out that maneuver, Drake?

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:51.850
The enemy ships have begun advancing toward Calais. Over.

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:57.230
As soon as the fire ships reach Calais, we will strike the enemy's main fleet!

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:06.240
This isn't right. Don't give chase, moron!

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:13.160
I knew this smelled fishy.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:16.120
Aren't sailors supposed to love their ships?!

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:18.880
Why are they approaching us?

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:19.670
They wouldn't...!

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:22.090
Everyone, go inside and take cover!

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:39.560
Those ships were filled with explosion spells and catalysts.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:44.320
Thus Tres España's armada truly did suffer a loss due to some fire ships.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:49.950
They used the reenactment of history against me...

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:50.830
How badly were we hit?

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.210
What gives?!

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:02.670
Here too...

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:05.510
They used a massive amount of spell talismans as chaff

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:08.010
to render the automated dolls' sensory perception inoperable.

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:10.590
That was low, wasn't it?

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:12.810
But I'm not done yet.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:18.730
The mechanical phoenixes that were dispatched to the New World?!

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:39.870
Are they using the confusion to turn this into a battle royal?

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.750
The army of Birnam slippeth from trees

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.550
hither and thither, hidden below their leafy boughs.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:50.590
With their main forces standing at the back,

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:53.260
they do strike the castle from all 'round.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:57.520
'Twas but to make Macbeth believe a formidable force approacheth as he hid behind castle walls.

00:08:57.520 --> 00:09:00.230
<i>O power, keep strong and press forward!</i>

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:02.940
None in the army of Birnam cowards be.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:03.940
<i>Keep low!</i>

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:06.690
<i>Slip through them and lay on the pressure!</i>

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:09.450
Men of Birnam, carry on the assault!

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:13.370
<i>Don't lose your cool!</i>

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:15.450
<i>I've always been an amateur!</i>

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:19.250
<i>Is she going all out?</i>

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:26.130
<i>It's the full cast from all of Shakespeare's plays!</i>

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:42.520
This is Shakespeare's masterpiece.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:46.520
Of the four great tragedies, it is called the ultimate play.

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:48.690
Isn't that...?

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:50.740
It's King Lear!

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:56.080
This combination of plays can be enjoyed anywhere in London, England.

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:57.660
Please enjoy the show.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:01.160
Stand, King of Britain.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:05.210
O King Lear, die as thou screamst over the loss of thy most beloved daughter, Cordelia.

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:09.340
Cast aside thy helplessness and die as thy howl ushereth victory!

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.480
Is that a ritual performance?

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:27.480
A writer up against Shakespeare's plays dedicated his works

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:31.490
to the God of Literature in exchange for that power.

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:35.990
The literature festival drew you here and now you've manifested yourself before an amateur writer

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:38.990
so you can get tipsy off of assimilating literature?

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:40.740
Well, Heavenly Deity Michizane?

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:50.710
Shall we edit each other's works?

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:53.130
Tes. Please don't die.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:55.090
Even in death, a pro continues to edit.

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:18.660
Masazumi?

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:21.660
Masazumi? You're not her.

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:24.660
The bandage smells of Masazumi.

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:28.630
Masazumi is in danger?

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:34.720
Don't know Masazumi?

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:40.850
<i>That's Masazumi's mouse!</i>

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:44.600
<i>It sensed that its master is in peril and wants to travel through the Earth Pulses...</i>

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:48.270
<i>But doesn't that require information on its target?</i>

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:49.520
We know her.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:50.690
We tell you.

00:11:50.690 --> 00:11:52.480
Save her! Save her!

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:54.490
Save Masazumi!

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:55.570
Masazumi.

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:56.360
Politician.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:57.740
Loves taxes.

00:11:57.740 --> 00:11:58.530
Cross-dresses.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:11:59.570
Doesn't stand out.

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:00.620
Poor.

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:01.740
Passes out.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:02.580
Cross-dresses.

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:08.670
<i>Hang in there!</i>

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:11.250
Forgot! She's a bad comedian.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.130
<i>Great! That's the latest info!</i>

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:27.730
Fall in Hell!

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:30.520
Fall in the Six Paths!

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:33.400
Are you really part of the Anglican Church?!

00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:35.820
Yes!

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:38.900
Now then, we're going to club you... to death!

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:41.950
I can't stand losing like this!

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:42.870
Masazumi!

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:46.160
Your mouse is on its way! Please accept it.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:47.040
What?! It isn't here!

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:48.460
The end! Death!
What?! It isn't here!

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:50.330
W-Wait! No!
The end! Death!

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:51.170
It isn't here!

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:53.790
Huh?

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:56.710
It's you!

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:00.760
In celebration of your mouse recognizing you as its master,

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:03.640
I sent it over with a load of offensive spells!

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:05.310
Won't they have a happy death?

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:07.020
Is that something a priestess should say?!

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:09.940
Boss, let's be calm about this!

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:11.940
Get them!

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:14.940
Oh, no!

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:23.570
As the Head of the Disciplinary Committee, surely you know.

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:25.490
Scaffold.

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:26.450
Judge.

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:30.460
Once, England executed a girl of a different species.

00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:35.670
It was the Maid of Orleans from Hexagone Française in the Hundred Years' War.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:39.550
Supposedly she wanted to die.

00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:42.510
The different beings that had fought along her side

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:45.850
took some of her artifacts from the execution grounds.

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:47.510
These chains were one of the items.

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:50.810
They possess the power to restrain angels

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:53.730
and were adapted to utilize the traits of an immortal.

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:56.610
They are a British-made intelligent item.

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:16.500
You have done well to return to the land of your birth on a full moon night,

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:21.010
when otherly beings' powers are at their peak, Silver Chains!

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:31.480
Musashi will save those who have resigned themselves to be executed!

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:41.740
Looking great!

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:48.490
Bite!

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:04.300
A mouse?

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:05.590
Help me!

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:09.470
You must be that automated doll's OS, yes?

00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:19.730
I will have to report to my King.

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:23.940
It's thanks to him I was able to win.

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:40.630
We're doomed!

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.050
Our Chancellor has come to fan the flames!

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:48.180
Hey, take a look at reality! We're screwed, Adele!

00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:50.550
Musashi is doomed!

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:51.310
Chancellor?

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:52.310
Yeah?

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:54.020
The viceroy is behind you.

00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:59.100
Uh, Chancellor?

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:01.570
Dummies shouldn't escalate things!

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:04.860
Aren't you pals with that group of doofs?

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:07.950
I can't do anything, but you guys can.

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:11.280
So why don't you twist history a bit more?

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:14.240
You know what to do at times like this, don't you?

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:16.910
Judge!

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:24.090
Someone, please save us!

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:26.760
What is that?

00:16:30.970 --> 00:16:32.680
They're using cargo ships as shields!

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:34.390
Please save—

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:35.810
Don't worry.
Please save—

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:38.190
We'll protect everyone with the power of money.

00:16:38.190 --> 00:16:39.980
My cargo ship!

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:41.940
It's where I hide my money from taxes!

00:16:41.940 --> 00:16:43.730
Why did you use my ship, too?

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:45.650
You bastard! What are you after?!

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:46.990
Let's get down to business!

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:51.200
We'll start with selling the rights to use defensive spells.

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:00.790
Herrlich!

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:07.550
Bore through the enemy!

00:17:08.510 --> 00:17:09.840
Here come the stakes!

00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:15.100
All automated dolls! Deactivate your sense of self and reboot!

00:17:15.100 --> 00:17:18.430
Everyone, rely only upon your intrinsic sensory devices.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:21.020
Communicate through divine transmissions or by mouth.

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:25.360
And as the unidentified Musashi, I shall reactivate the gravity barriers. Over.

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:31.410
Receive, maid-style!

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:43.500
A-Are you okay?

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:44.790
Y-Yeah!

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:45.790
Adele!

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:47.250
I've got an idea!

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:49.880
An idea? What is it?

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:53.390
<i>They seem to be on top of things.</i>

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:55.260
So? What do you think?

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:57.060
We don't have any other choice, do we?

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.810
The ships are rising when they should be immobile!

00:18:08.070 --> 00:18:11.490
They're individually steering Musashi's eight ships to pull them apart!

00:18:11.490 --> 00:18:13.740
How are they doing that when the automated dolls aren't linked?!

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:15.740
Over here! Over here!

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:23.960
This should work!

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:25.920
Make sure none of the vessels stay in one place!

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:27.380
And fire the cannons!

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:30.340
Commence firing the cannons. Over.

00:18:34.930 --> 00:18:37.640
So, they've turned this into a war of attrition then?

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:40.100
Admiral! We aren't done yet, remember?!

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:43.270
Yes, the true battle begins as we retreat.

00:18:43.270 --> 00:18:48.820
But the end result will be something <i>we</i> brought about!

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:49.820
Yeah!

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:03.370
O king, brandish thy sword and smite he who wieldeth power!

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:07.580
<i>O powers, receive the blow! This is your final opponent!</i>

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:14.680
<i>Hey! "Your final opponent shall be him," sounds better.</i>

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:17.390
<i>Really?</i>

00:19:17.390 --> 00:19:21.180
<i>Yep! I think it'd be more effective if you inverted the sentence.</i>

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:25.560
<i>That aside, want to talk bout the last play we saw?</i>

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:29.110
<i>In that case, I'd rather discuss the book I just read.</i>

00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:31.150
<i>Tell me about both of them!</i>

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:35.200
<i>I'm pretty sure I left off where he was reunited with Vergilius.</i>

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:37.280
<i>When did you read this?</i>

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:39.160
<i>You forgot?</i>

00:19:39.160 --> 00:19:42.160
<i>I just read it last week.</i>

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:47.250
<i>Weren't we both in the library that entire day?</i>

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:49.630
I just remembered something.

00:19:50.090 --> 00:19:51.290
What?

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:56.090
When you were with me, you used a different form of speech.

00:19:57.630 --> 00:19:59.640
When did it change?

00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:03.640
That happened after you left!

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:07.690
O king, howl! Grieve thine errors.

00:20:08.650 --> 00:20:11.520
O power, reach out to the kings' righteousness!

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:17.700
Even if that righteousness gives birth to tragedy?

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:19.320
So what if it does?!

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:24.910
O king, test to see if such righteousness is worth possessing!

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:27.040
I swear I will go there!

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:30.250
I will go to the place where we once saw righteousness together!

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:31.960
Then what about me?

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:33.630
Where did I go?!

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:46.770
The king wept.

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:49.520
With his beloved daughter's body cradled in arms,

00:20:49.520 --> 00:20:52.060
his own righteousness made him howl.

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:55.280
The power will stop his righteousness.

00:20:56.070 --> 00:20:59.740
Go, usurper to the throne! Save the king!

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:00.660
That's impossible!

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:02.660
It isn't impossible! It's called editing!

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:05.330
It's something that I can do because I'm in your play.

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:09.080
I used a spell to take Macbeth apart and rewrite it!

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:17.460
A Macbeth that is determined to usurp the throne?!

00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:19.970
Stories are flexible.

00:21:19.970 --> 00:21:23.720
You can even use that as the groundwork to make a different story.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:25.470
Go, Macbeth!

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:27.430
Stop this tragedy through your own victory!

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:43.910
Smile, O king!

00:21:44.910 --> 00:21:47.740
The usurper is with the king!

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:56.290
Which one am I?

00:21:59.010 --> 00:22:02.010
Why not be the one who liked me?

00:22:02.010 --> 00:22:04.140
Eh?! Wait, what?

00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:05.760
Where'd that come from?!

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:08.930
After all, I'm right here.

00:22:09.980 --> 00:22:11.560
Where are you?

00:22:15.310 --> 00:22:16.440
Here.

00:22:26.200 --> 00:22:28.120
I don't need this anymore.

00:22:28.120 --> 00:22:30.250
I've seen most of the criticism out there anyway.

00:22:30.790 --> 00:22:34.000
You're probably going to need this in the future.

00:22:35.630 --> 00:22:36.630
You sure?

00:22:36.630 --> 00:22:38.170
Won't they revoke your inherited name?

00:22:38.460 --> 00:22:42.170
In actuality, King Lear was saved by his youngest daughter Cordelia

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:43.930
and was peacefully restored to the throne.

00:22:43.930 --> 00:22:47.970
Shakespeare altered that to make it a tragedy.

00:22:47.970 --> 00:22:51.270
So the only one who can succeed Shakespeare's name is me,

00:22:51.270 --> 00:22:54.270
since I have experienced something that surpasses that.

00:22:57.480 --> 00:23:00.030
Hey, could you look over there for a second?

00:23:03.650 --> 00:23:05.740
Wh-What? Why'd you do that?

00:23:05.740 --> 00:23:08.450
I stole the Armament of Deadly Sins from you!

00:23:09.120 --> 00:23:11.240
I <i>am</i> Macbeth after all!

00:23:15.420 --> 00:23:17.130
Hear that? The audience is giving their applause.

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:24.420
Then do you think it'd be okay if the King wanted to stay with Macbeth?

00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:40.360
It would seem the city has become quite lively.

00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:42.360
Fairy Queen!

00:23:42.730 --> 00:23:44.820
Let's play a game, Mary.

00:23:44.820 --> 00:23:48.320
Let's enjoy the game we used to play with Father long ago.

00:23:48.320 --> 00:23:52.410
This time it will be with the fool who may possibly come.

00:23:53.950 --> 00:23:55.120
There you are!

00:23:59.670 --> 00:24:01.800
We'll see whether or not he wins you some time.

00:24:02.670 --> 00:24:04.010
Those are the stakes.
